      "vote": "3-0 (Fenwick J., Garrow J., Holt J., unanimous on all four questions): POSITION A - REQUIRE RESOLUTION AS INTERPRETATION - prevails. Requiring a declared assent_source to resolve to a real, digest-matched, covering Sovereign-assent event is faithful interpretation of the entrenched term \"valid\" as ACT-COMPUTER-FIRST-REALM s.23 (imported by ACT-ASSENTED-RECORD-PROTECTION s.1 \"within the meaning of s.23\" and given continuing deterministic effect by INV-ASSENT-SOURCE-001) already defines it, and is within the Privy Council's interpretive power. It is NOT an amendment of the entrenched floor: it changes no word of VJS-ACT 10, s.23, or INV-ASSENT-SOURCE-001, removes protection from no genuinely-assented record, and therefore is NOT routed to the Sovereign for assent. Position B (value-on-the-allow-list suffices; the cure is a Sovereign amendment) is REJECTED as the reading that, contrary to its own claim, would amend the entrenched text by nullifying s.23's resolution verbs. Position C's belt-and-braces reserved-amendment limb is REJECTED on constitutional hygiene (it would imply the entrenched meaning was contingent on a confirming Act, corroding the meaning it confirms); the Sovereign retains the prerogative to place the requirement beyond future argument by an express Act, but the cure is effective on this order and is not conditional on any such Act. No dissent."
