      "path": "Judicature/.justice/judgments/supreme-court/2026-realm-sc-11.md",
      "pdf": "",
      "points": [
        "Enacts CASE-LAW s.24 (ordinary, declaratory; unanimous it is ordinary not constitutional) - persuasive only in V2.",
        "Condition 1 - Unity and currency of law: applies the canonical CASE-LAW, VPR, bench and duty unaltered, mints no local statute, and renders the central text LIVE as the apex enacts it - never a vendored, pinned, or stale local copy (else it mints a subscribed local jurisdiction under s.9).",
        "Condition 2 - Unity of citator and apex: every binding decision resolves to the one central citation series and single central apex; no parallel series or local apex.",
        "Condition 3 - The synthesiser bar: the client constitutes no deciding bench of its own; it only displays rulings handed down by a properly constituted central bench.",
        "Condition 4 - Delivery not law-making: the client force is engineering (rendering), deriving wholly from the canonical organ, never from promulgation by the client (source-of-force test, REALM-SC 8).",
        "Condition 5 - Candour of provenance: the re-skinned nomenclature is disclosed to the user as descriptive presentation of canonical VJS governance, not an independent locally-sovereign body.",
        "Condition 6 (7:2) - External-law floor / non-impersonation: the client must not wear the appearance of a regulated real-world legal authority it does not hold (grounded in REALM-SC 9); a floor of substance, not a script of UI wording.",
        "Ownership of the renderer is not ownership of the law; the vendor controls when canonical law is displayed, never what it is."
      ],
      "question": "Is an embeddable governance client rendering canonical law from a central server a lawful presentation-layer division or a forbidden parallel court?",
      "status": "good-law",
      "summary": "Full court (leapfrog): an embeddable, corporate-re-skinned client that renders the same canonical governance from a central server of law is a lawful presentation DIVISION over the one spine, not a forbidden parallel COURT, only on six cumulative conditions. Re-naming canonical governance is permitted; re-housing substantive law, citator, bench, or apex inside the product is forbidden. Public-only record: the confidential client matter is withheld; persuasive in V2, not binding unless incorporated.",
      "superseded_by": [],
      "supersedes": [],
      "title": "The Server-of-Law and the Embeddable Governance Client",
